From 1d77d15bd4237c086e7803de54c609f0b3365017 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: allcodernet <67543055+allcodernet@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 18:29:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 15/45] decide-compat: Jev /v1/systemone translation library
 and error.field

Add decide-compat.{h,cpp} to llama-decide: pure functions that translate a
Jev System One request into a /v1/decide body (spec 3.1-3.2, 422 shape
errors as compat_error with a loc built from JSON keys), a /v1/decide
response into the Jev response (3.3), the demo confidence approximation,
and the FastAPI {"detail": [...]} error bodies.

decide::error gains an optional field member: compile() stamps the field
name on errors raised inside a field, build_trie sets it at the three
throw sites that name the field, and error_result adds "field" to the
{"error": {...}} body when it is non-empty.

test-decide-compat covers request and response translation, the 422 locs,
confidence values and the error mapping; no model needed.
